From 95cd4936373a83cd8ccc365b547e7c8603d60676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corpus review <review@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:20:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Fix study-note plates: readable structure-label list,
 honest note chips, larger preview, tissue lenses

- renderStage(): move the 'Structure labels' disclosure out of the dark image
  stage so it is no longer clipped over the plate and its dark-teal summary is
  readable again.
- miniChip(): study notes with no pin and no lens show a neutral note glyph
  instead of the same random crop of the chapter plate on every row.
- preview.js: taller preview budget for tall plates and a shorter crop, so the
  enlarged image and the 'Closer look' crop both fit without hunting inside the dialog.
- styles.css: card styling for the relocated label list, note chip, crop cap.
- micro-lens.js: tissue lenses for foundations, heart myocardium, brain cortical
  layers, cerebellar cortex and the 2/4/8-cell, morula and blastocyst parts, all
  reusing renders that already ship (no new image weight).
- Sidebar overview box now labels its value 'Location' and switches to 'Function'
  only when a part is selected.
